@startuml network_variation_sequence
title bridgeIQ — Whole Game VARIATION: Networked play (biq<->biq lobby; Q-NET deferred)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
actor "Host user" as Host
participant "MainWindow\n(host)" as MWh
participant "NetworkController" as NET
participant "MainWindow\n(guest)" as MWg
actor "Guest user" as Guest

== Lobby: biq <-> biq (native JSON protocol) ==
Host -> MWh : Network > Start Server
MWh -> NET : start_server(port, name, seat)
NET --> MWh : server_started -> NetworkLobbyDialog (live seat map)

Guest -> MWg : Network > Connect to Server
MWg -> NET : connect_to_server(host, port, name)
NET -> NET : CONNECT_REQUEST / CONNECT_ACCEPT
NET --> MWg : connection_established -> _on_network_connected()
Guest -> MWg : click seat -> request_seat()  (SEAT_REQUEST)
NET --> MWh : client_joined / seat_map_changed

Host -> MWh : "Start Game"
MWh -> NET : start_game()  (GAME_START broadcast)
MWh -> MWh : _start_network_game()

== Deal + bidding (host authoritative) ==
MWh -> NET : new_deal() ; broadcast_deal(board)  (DEAL_START)
NET --> MWg : deal_received -> phase='bidding'
note over MWh, MWg
  Each seat owned by exactly one app instance.
  Local turn  -> human/AI bids, then broadcast_bid() (BID_MADE).
  Remote turn -> wait, then remote_bid_received -> _on_network_remote_bid().
  Same pattern for cards: broadcast_card() / remote_card_received,
  dummy reveal (broadcast_dummy_reveal), and the "Next Card"
  ack (broadcast_trick_clear / trick_clear_received).
end note

== End of board / scoring ==
MWh -> MWh : _show_result() (+ teams: start_closed_room_async)
MWh -> NET : broadcast_closed_room_ingested(run)  (CLOSED_ROOM_INGESTED)
NET --> MWg : closed_room_ingested -> scoring_table comparison row

== SEPARATE PATH (deferred): Q-NET server, Q-Plus as client ==
note over MWh, NET
  Distinct from the biq<->biq JSON lobby above. Q-Plus speaks Q-NET
  (bracketed text tokens), NOT biq's JSON. Plan: wrap the proven
  tools/biq_qnet_server.py BiqServer in a QThread whose callbacks
  {status, deal, bid, contract, card, board_done} emit Qt signals
  to drive the same TableView + status strip.
  STATUS: BiqServer callbacks DONE; QThread + GUI action TO BUILD.
  Q-Plus-as-server + biq client (tools/biq_qnet_client.py) is the
  proven, already-working measurement path.
end note
@enduml
